                <pb facs="1136" n="1016" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg1016"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/733: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-16T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>16. Your March 15, 11 a.m. Department approves discussion with Mr. Morrow, and,
                    if you deem it advisable, with President Zayas, of scheme for examination and
                    statement of national finances, and for new system of public accounting. It is
                    believed that adequate accounting system should be specifically emphasized,
                    pointing out that such system is necessary to enable both bankers and American
                    Government to give proper consideration to question of permanent loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
